{"slug":"running-sum","title":"Running Sum","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":102,"tags":["arrays","prefix-sum"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Prefix sums","body":["The **prefix sum** at position `i` is the sum of all elements from the start up to and including `i`. All prefix sums can be produced in one pass, because each one is the previous prefix sum plus the new element.",{"code":"total = 0\nfor x in a:\n    total += x\n    # total is now the prefix sum at this element"},"Prefix sums are one of the most useful tools for arrays. The next problems use them to answer many \"sum of a part of the array\" questions quickly."]},"statement":["Given an array of `n` integers, print its running sums: the i-th printed number is the sum of the first i numbers of the array."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["Print `n` integers separated by spaces."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^6 <= each number <= 10^6"],"examples":[{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"1 3 6 10 15\n","note":"1, 1+2, 1+2+3, ..."}],"hints":["The answer for position i needs the answer for position i - 1.","Keep one variable `total` and add each element to it.","Print `total` after adding each element."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Each prefix sum is the previous one plus the current element, so one running variable is enough."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1) besides the output.","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\ntotal = 0\nout = []\nfor x in a:\n    total += x\n    out.append(total)\nprint(*out)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        total += a[i];\n        cout << total << (i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        long total = 0;\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            total += a[i];\n            sb.append(total).append(i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"1\n5\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"1\n-5\n","output":"-5\n"},{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"1 3 6 10 15\n"},{"input":"4\n-1 1 -1 1\n","output":"-1 0 -1 0\n"},{"input":"3\n1000000 1000000 1000000\n","output":"1000000 2000000 3000000\n"},{"input":"30\n38 9 51 98 85 42 37 61 -2 -69 4 85 63 62 42 62 -36 19 -79 -9 34 76 -18 -3 84 52 -45 67 -44 47\n","output":"38 47 98 196 281 323 360 421 419 350 354 439 502 564 606 668 632 651 572 563 597 673 655 652 736 788 743 810 766 813\n"},{"input":"1000\n-434507 -884144 -18872 -740405 993244 -774239 -78820 826101 -778080 -24155 -119595 -166379 -863733 470120 -106344 466136 -629511 -529339 698631 -141987 926454 916860 -301252 836927 949957 -451248 422935 -361708 -138172 -702455 636450 39865 -418148 2